# --- Wave B1 shape-drain: causal-link cardinality restorations ---
# gmeow:CausalLinkShape — exactly one antecedent EventType, one consequent EventType, at most
# one decimal link strength, and exactly one causal modality. gmeow:causalModality is
# OWL FunctionalProperty, but the functional maximum rides a gmeow:causalModality-keyed
# subjects-of shape, not the CausalLink node shape — so the exactly-one obligation the shape
# authored declaratively is restored here as an ordinary logic:maxQualifiedCardinality (min1 comes
# from the migrated existence closure). gmeow:linkMechanism's per-language-tag uniqueness is
# grounded declaratively by gmeow:CausalLinkMechanismUniqueLangConstraint below.
gmeow:CausalLink logic:subClassOf
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:linkAntecedent ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass logic:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:linkConsequent ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass logic:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:causalModality ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass logic:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:linkStrength ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange xsd:decimal ] .

# gmeow:CausalLinkShape — gmeow:linkMechanism carries at most one value per language tag (the
# localizable-prose per-language-tag uniqueness convention). A declarative logic: sugar record grounds the sh:uniqueLang
# facet: the frontend derives a sh:uniqueLang property component on the gmeow:CausalLink node shape.
gmeow:CausalLinkMechanismUniqueLangConstraint
    a logic:UniqueLangConstraint ;
    rdfs:label "CausalLink mechanism unique-language constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/risk> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: a gmeow:CausalLink carries at most one gmeow:linkMechanism per language tag (no two language-tagged values share a tag)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:onClass gmeow:CausalLink ;
    logic:valuePath gmeow:linkMechanism ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:CausalLinkShape ;
    logic:message "A CausalLink carries at most one gmeow:linkMechanism per language tag (localizable prose, the per-language-tag uniqueness convention)." .

# ── logic: assertion carriers for this slice's own terms ────────────────────────
# The canonical logic: carriers for the characteristics and integrity conditions of the
# terms THIS slice owns. Each record names one of this slice's own properties or classes
# through a logic: RBox predicate; the native coherence gate joins the record to enforce
# the condition, and the OWL grounding view projects OWL FunctionalProperty (and friends)
# from it. Authored here rather than in the logic slice because the fact asserted is a
# fact about this slice's own term, and a grounding slice never depends on a non-grounding
# slice (docs/GROUNDING.md, the tier rule): the logic: assertion vocabulary is CONSUMED
# here (gmeow:sliceDependsOn logic), never owned.
#   logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion — logic:characterizes names the property, logic:characteristicSort its characteristic.
#   logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion — the two logic:distinctnessRole values must bind distinct relata on one focus node.

gmeow:cascadeFirstLinkFunctionality
    a logic:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/risk> ;
    rdfs:label "cascadeFirstLink is functional"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:cascadeFirstLink is functional: a cascade has exactly one entry link, the single causal link at which a walk of the named failure chain begins. This record is not a definition of that term and never a shape: the obligation is reasoned from the record, not restated elsewhere."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:characterizes gmeow:cascadeFirstLink ;
    logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:cascadeFirstLink ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the native coherence gate must enforce that gmeow:cascadeFirstLink names exactly one value; this record is the canonical carrier the gate joins, so the obligation is reasoned rather than restated on a shape surface."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid this record when a second value would make the record ambiguous — retire the assertion instead of weakening it, and never mirror it as a hand-authored shape."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Read together with logic:characteristicSort: the pair (logic:characterizes gmeow:cascadeFirstLink, logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty) is the whole obligation, and the OWL grounding view projects the matching characteristic from it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this record carries ONE integrity obligation about gmeow:cascadeFirstLink and nothing else. It is not a definition of gmeow:cascadeFirstLink (that lives on the term itself), not a shape, and not a second place to state the term's meaning — retire the record rather than broaden it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:cascadeFirstLinkFunctionality logic:characterizes gmeow:cascadeFirstLink ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .
gmeow:causalModalityFunctionality
    a logic:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/risk> ;
    rdfs:label "causalModality is functional"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:causalModality is functional: a causal link claims exactly one force — necessitates, promotes, enables, or prevents — the single modality that is the very reason the link was reified. This record is not a definition of that term and never a shape: the obligation is reasoned from the record, not restated elsewhere."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:characterizes gmeow:causalModality ;
    logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:causalModality ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the native coherence gate must enforce that gmeow:causalModality names exactly one value; this record is the canonical carrier the gate joins, so the obligation is reasoned rather than restated on a shape surface."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid this record when a second value would make the record ambiguous — retire the assertion instead of weakening it, and never mirror it as a hand-authored shape."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Read together with logic:characteristicSort: the pair (logic:characterizes gmeow:causalModality, logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty) is the whole obligation, and the OWL grounding view projects the matching characteristic from it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this record carries ONE integrity obligation about gmeow:causalModality and nothing else. It is not a definition of gmeow:causalModality (that lives on the term itself), not a shape, and not a second place to state the term's meaning — retire the record rather than broaden it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:causalModalityFunctionality logic:characterizes gmeow:causalModality ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .
gmeow:hazardBearerFunctionality
    a logic:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/risk> ;
    rdfs:label "hazardBearer is functional"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:hazardBearer is functional: a hazard inheres in exactly one bearer, per gUFO inherence — the same danger borne by two systems is two hazards, not one shared between them."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:characterizes gmeow:hazardBearer ;
    logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:hazardBearer ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the native coherence gate must enforce that gmeow:hazardBearer names exactly one value; this record is the canonical carrier the gate joins, so the obligation is reasoned rather than restated on a shape surface."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid this record when a second value would make the record ambiguous — retire the assertion instead of weakening it, and never mirror it as a hand-authored shape."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Read together with logic:characteristicSort: the pair (logic:characterizes gmeow:hazardBearer, logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty) is the whole obligation, and the OWL grounding view projects the matching characteristic from it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this record carries ONE integrity obligation about gmeow:hazardBearer and nothing else. It is not a definition of gmeow:hazardBearer (that lives on the term itself), not a shape, and not a second place to state the term's meaning — retire the record rather than broaden it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:hazardBearerFunctionality logic:characterizes gmeow:hazardBearer ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .
gmeow:linkAntecedentFunctionality
    a logic:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/risk> ;
    rdfs:label "linkAntecedent is functional"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:linkAntecedent is functional: a causal link has exactly one causing kind, the single antecedent event type, held distinct from the consequent so that nothing type-causes itself."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:characterizes gmeow:linkAntecedent ;
    logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:linkAntecedent ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the native coherence gate must enforce that gmeow:linkAntecedent names exactly one value; this record is the canonical carrier the gate joins, so the obligation is reasoned rather than restated on a shape surface."@x-gmeow-english ;
