gmeow:linkNextAcyclicity
    a logic:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/risk> ;
    rdfs:label "linkNext is acyclic"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:linkNext is acyclic: a causal-cascade walk never reaches itself through gmeow:linkNext, as the Cascade prose states. linkNext is deliberately NOT transitive (it names the immediate next link, not every downstream one), so the native coherence gate enforces this with an internal reachability walk that raises a violation on any cycle, never by materialising the closure; the generated SHACL constraint surface is its projection."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:characterizes gmeow:linkNext ;
    logic:characteristicSort logic:acyclicProperty ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:linkNext ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the native coherence gate must enforce that gmeow:linkNext admits no cycle; this record is the canonical carrier the gate joins, so the obligation is reasoned rather than restated on a shape surface."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid this record when a cycle is a legitimate shape — retire the assertion instead of weakening it, and never mirror it as a hand-authored shape."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Read together with logic:characteristicSort: the pair (logic:characterizes gmeow:linkNext, logic:characteristicSort logic:acyclicProperty) is the whole obligation, and the OWL grounding view projects the matching characteristic from it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this record carries ONE integrity obligation about gmeow:linkNext and nothing else. It is not a definition of gmeow:linkNext (that lives on the term itself), not a shape, and not a second place to state the term's meaning — retire the record rather than broaden it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:linkNextAcyclicity logic:characterizes gmeow:linkNext ."@x-gmeow-english ;
